    {
      "slug": "vintage-william-morris-dinosaur-pattern",
      "deletedAt": "2026-10-30T10:49:59.964Z",
      "reason": "Ручное перемещение в корзину",
      "originalIndex": 0,
      "product": {
        "slug": "vintage-william-morris-dinosaur-pattern",
        "title": "Vintage William Morris Dinosaur Pattern",
        "author": "clipArtem",
        "canonical": "https://www.creativefabrica.com/product/vintage-william-morris-dinosaur-pattern/",
        "url": "https://www.creativefabrica.com/product/vintage-william-morris-dinosaur-pattern/",
        "description": "Dusty rose triceratops and sage green brachiosaurus woven into an ornate William Morris-style damask — a sophisticated gender-neutral nursery print in muted antique tones.\nThis stunning surface pattern fuses prehistoric creatures with classical Renaissance-inspired foliage scrollwork, creating an unexpected yet perfectly harmonious design. A large triceratops rendered in dusty rose takes center stage, flanked by long-necked brachiosaurus dinosaurs in muted sage green. Elaborate acanthus leaf scrolls, fern fronds, and stylized lotus-like blooms weave throughout the composition in sage, olive, gold, and blush pink against a warm cream ivory background. The overall aesthetic channels William Morris Arts and Crafts movement sensibility reimagined for the modern nursery or children’s space.\nThe colour story is intentionally restrained and sophisticated — dusty rose, sage green, warm taupe, antique gold, blush pink, and ivory cream combine to produce a vintage, almost watercolour-washed mood that skews far from typical bright primary-colour dinosaur prints. This makes the pattern exceptionally versatile for gender-neutral nursery decor, boho children’s room wallpaper, premium fabric yardage, sublimation blankets and pillows, gift wrapping paper, scrapbooking collections, and stationery suites. Digital crafters will find it ideal for Procreate brushes, Photoshop mockups, Canva templates, and POD product uploads on Redbubble, Spoonflower, and Society6.",
        "fullDescription": "<p>Dusty rose triceratops and sage green brachiosaurus woven into an ornate William Morris-style damask — a sophisticated gender-neutral nursery print in muted antique tones.</p>\n<p>This stunning surface pattern fuses prehistoric creatures with classical Renaissance-inspired foliage scrollwork, creating an unexpected yet perfectly harmonious design. A large triceratops rendered in dusty rose takes center stage, flanked by long-necked brachiosaurus dinosaurs in muted sage green. Elaborate acanthus leaf scrolls, fern fronds, and stylized lotus-like blooms weave throughout the composition in sage, olive, gold, and blush pink against a warm cream ivory background. The overall aesthetic channels William Morris Arts and Crafts movement sensibility reimagined for the modern nursery or children’s space.</p>\n<p>The colour story is intentionally restrained and sophisticated — dusty rose, sage green, warm taupe, antique gold, blush pink, and ivory cream combine to produce a vintage, almost watercolour-washed mood that skews far from typical bright primary-colour dinosaur prints. This makes the pattern exceptionally versatile for gender-neutral nursery decor, boho children’s room wallpaper, premium fabric yardage, sublimation blankets and pillows, gift wrapping paper, scrapbooking collections, and stationery suites. Digital crafters will find it ideal for Procreate brushes, Photoshop mockups, Canva templates, and POD product uploads on Redbubble, Spoonflower, and Society6.</p>",
